<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch ban Swiss cattle imports in BSE scare.</title>
<headline>Dutch ban Swiss cattle imports in BSE scare.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Netherlands said on Wednesday it was banning all cattle imports from Switzerland, because of fears over mad cow disease.</p>
<p>In a brief statement, the agriculture ministry said the ban, which comes into force on Thursday, had been prompted by a recent flood of Swiss cattle to The Netherlands while Swiss authorities considered what measures to take to combat Bovine Spongiform Encephalopathy (BSE).</p>
<p>After Britain, Switzerland has had the highest number of reported cases of BSE, the ministry statement said.</p>
<p>The Dutch do not normally import many Swiss cattle, but the prospect of a Swiss clampdown on cattle trade led to a surge in Dutch imports last month, to around 400 head, it said.</p>
<p>The ministry said it was taking its action as there was no likelihood of joint European Union measures in the near term. No-one at the ministry was available to give further details.</p>
</text>
